  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1201 PM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nThe synoptic pattern will finally begin to change over the weekend \nas broad troughing overspreads the western CONUS. At first, this \nwill result in a building of the ridge aloft over our area as \nHurricane Isaias makes landfall over the central Gulf Coast and \npulls northward. The Sat-Mon period is therefore expected to be even \nwarmer than this past week with highs ranging from the mid 80s to \nmid 90s under continued clear skies and with stronger SSW surface \nflow. By the middle of next week, the ridging aloft is progged to \nshift eastward which will allow an increase in SW flow aloft over \nWest TX. A fairly large subset of ensemble members suggest that this \nevolution combined with an increasing fetch of Pacific tropical \nmoisture could bring more widespread shower activity to the region \nduring the Tue-Thu timeframe, but with temperatures still likely to \nremain above average.",
